<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">10 November in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">8 events that happened on 10 November, from 1202 to 1975.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/fourth-crusade" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/fourth-crusade.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1202 CE <span class="tih-ago">824 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Fourth Crusade lays siege to the Christian city of Zara</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crusader-states">Crusaders</a> unable to pay the Venetians for their fleet arrived at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zadar">Zara</a> on the Dalmatian coast and besieged it for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/venice">Venice</a>. The city fell within two weeks, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pope-innocent-iii">Pope Innocent III</a> excommunicated the crusaders.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/republic-of-venice">Republic of Venice</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fourth-crusade">Fourth Crusade</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1293">1293 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">733 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Raden Wijaya is crowned the first king of Majapahit</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/raden-wijaya">Raden Wijaya</a>, who had used a Mongol expedition sent by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kublai-khan">Kublai Khan</a> to defeat his rivals and then driven the Mongol forces out, was crowned the first ruler of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/majapahit-empire">Majapahit</a> in eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/java">Java</a>, taking the name Kertarajasa Jayawardhana.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/raden-wijaya">Raden Wijaya</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/majapahit-empire">Majapahit Empire</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1444">1444 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">582 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Sultan Murad II defeats the crusaders at Varna</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The Ottoman army of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sultan">Sultan</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/murad-ii">Murad II</a> defeated a crusading army of Hungarians, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poles">Poles</a> and Wallachians near the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/black-sea">Black Sea</a> port of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/varna">Varna</a>. King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wladyslaw-iii-of-poland">Władysław III of Poland</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hungary">Hungary</a> was killed, and the defeat ended the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crusade-of-varna">Crusade of Varna</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-varna">Battle of Varna</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wladyslaw-iii-of-poland">Władysław III of Poland</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/murad-ii">Murad II</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1599">1599 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">427 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Supporters of Sigismund III Vasa are executed in the Åbo Bloodbath</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">In the final phase of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sweden">Sweden</a>'s civil war, supporters of the deposed King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sigismund-iii-vasa">Sigismund III Vasa</a> were publicly executed at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/turku">Turku</a> (Åbo) in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/finland">Finland</a>. Duke Charles of Södermanland, the later Charles IX, was crushing the last resistance to his rule.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sigismund-iii-vasa">Sigismund III Vasa</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1775">1775 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">251 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Continental Congress creates the Continental Marines</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/continental-congress">Continental Congress</a> resolved to raise two battalions of Marines. The date is celebrated as the birthday of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states-marine-corps">United States Marine Corps</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1871">1871 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">155 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Henry Morton Stanley finds David Livingstone at Ujiji</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The journalist <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-morton-stanley">Henry Morton Stanley</a> located the missionary-explorer <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/david-livingstone">David Livingstone</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ujiji">Ujiji</a>, on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lake-tanganyika">Lake Tanganyika</a>, by Stanley's own dating. His reported greeting, 'Dr Livingstone, I presume?', became famous.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lake-tanganyika">Lake Tanganyika</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1938">1938 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">88 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Mustafa Kemal Atatürk dies in Istanbul</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Atatürk, founder and first president of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/republic-of-turkey">Republic of Turkey</a>, died at Dolmabahçe Palace. Turks still pause at 9.05 in the morning on this day to mark the moment of his death.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mustafa-kemal-ataturk">Mustafa Kemal Atatürk</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/republic-of-turkey">Republic of Turkey</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/istanbul">Istanbul</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1975">1975 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">51 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The freighter Edmund Fitzgerald sinks in Lake Superior</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The ore carrier SS Edmund Fitzgerald sank in a violent storm on Lake Superior with the loss of all 29 crew. It is the largest ship lost on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/great-lakes">Great Lakes</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/great-lakes">Great Lakes</a></div></div></li></ol>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-born"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-born">Born on 10 November <span class="n">9</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/philip-i-of-taranto"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/philip-i-of-taranto.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Philip I of Taranto</span><span class="tp">1278–1331</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/charles-the-bold"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/charles-the-bold.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Charles the Bold</span><span class="tp">1433–1477</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/martin-luther"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/martin-luther.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Martin Luther</span><span class="tp">1483–1546</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/henry-v-duke-of-brunswick-luneburg"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/henry-v-duke-of-brunswick-luneburg.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Henry V, Duke of Brunswick-Lüneburg</span><span class="tp">1489–1568</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/john-iii-duke-of-cleves"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/john-iii-duke-of-cleves.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">John III, Duke of Cleves</span><span class="tp">1490–1539</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/oliver-goldsmith"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/oliver-goldsmith.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Oliver Goldsmith</span><span class="tp">1728–1774</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/granville-sharp"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/granville-sharp.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Granville Sharp</span><span class="tp">1735–1813</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/friedrich-schiller"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/friedrich-schiller.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Friedrich Schiller</span><span class="tp">1759–1805</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/askar-akayev"><span class="ph ph-person" aria-hidden="true"></span><span><span class="nm">Askar Akayev</span><span class="tp">b. 1944</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-died"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-died">Died on 10 November <span class="n">7</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/godred-olafsson"><span class="ph ph-person" aria-hidden="true"></span><span><span class="nm">Godred Olafsson</span><span class="tp">d. 1187</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/wladyslaw-iii-of-poland"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/wladyslaw-iii-of-poland.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Władysław III of Poland</span><span class="tp">1424–1444</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/pope-paul-iii"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/pope-paul-iii.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Pope Paul III</span><span class="tp">1468–1549</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/afzal-khan-general"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/afzal-khan-general.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Afzal Khan (general)</span><span class="tp">d. 1659</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/louis-gustave-binger"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/louis-gustave-binger.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Louis-Gustave Binger</span><span class="tp">1856–1936</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/leonid-brezhnev"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/leonid-brezhnev.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Leonid Brezhnev</span><span class="tp">1906–1982</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/helmut-schmidt"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/helmut-schmidt.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Helmut Schmidt</span><span class="tp">1918–2015</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<p class="day-ppl-note">Dates as the sources give them: in the Julian calendar before 1582, and in some countries for longer (Britain until 1752, Russia until 1918). Only people whose day of birth or death the records agree on are listed.</p>
